cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SDV-BMT in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SDV-BMT: Model-level Accelerator Benchmark Core"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: Apache-2.0
# repository-code: to be added once the public repository URL is known.
abstract: >-
  SDV-BMT is a research benchmark framework for Model-level accelerator measurements. A C++ native
  measurement plane records per-request execution facts into append-only evidence bundles; a Python plane
  evaluates them into the Model-level Metric Set v1 and checks contrast validity with Design, Realization
  and Measurement Guards. Version 0.1.0 includes an NVIDIA GPU reference backend and a YOLOX-S / COCO
  reference workload. Its measurements do not establish WCET, FTTI, functional-safety compliance or
  vehicle-level safety.
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Boryoung
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - accelerator
  - automotive
  - software-defined vehicle
  - latency
  - evidence
